RECORD = HEAD THETHREEREFERENCES ETAGFORMS CONDITIONALHEADERSASGUARDS CONTENTRANGEASMODREDUCTION THETHREELEVELERRORTAXONOMY DATELASTMODIFIEDEXPIRESASTEMPORALFRAMES THETHREEREFERENCESMAPTOTHEVAULTSHEADTAILVALUE THEWILDCARDCONDITION .

HEAD =
  "// i138.ts — I-138: HTTP/1.1 headers as the three-reference index"
  "import assert from ""node:assert"";"
  .

THETHREEREFERENCES =
  "// ── 1. The three references ──────────────────────────────────────"
  "type Headers = Record<string, string>;"
  "// forward: Location (where to go next)"
  "const redirect: Headers = {"
  "  ""Location"": ""http://www.w3.org/pub/WWW/People.html"","
  "};"
  "// back: Content-Location (where this came from)"
  "const origin: Headers = {"
  "  ""Content-Location"": ""/pub/WWW/People.html"","
  "};"
  "// content-addressed: ETag (what this is)"
  "const tagged: Headers = {"
  "  ""ETag"": '""xyzzy""',"
  "};"
  "assert.ok(""Location"" in redirect,          ""Location = forward ref"");"
  "assert.ok(""Content-Location"" in origin,    ""Content-Location = back ref"");"
  "assert.ok(""ETag"" in tagged,                ""ETag = content address"");"
  "// a single response can carry both Location and Content-Location"
  "const both: Headers = {"
  "  ""Location"": ""http://new.example.com/x"","
  "  ""Content-Location"": ""http://old.example.com/x"","
  "  ""ETag"": '""v1""',"
  "};"
  "assert.strictEqual(Object.keys(both).length, 3, ""three refs in one response"");"
  .

ETAGFORMS =
  "// ── 2. ETag forms ────────────────────────────────────────────────"
  "const etags = ['""xyzzy""', 'W/""xyzzy""', '""""'];"
  "for (const et of etags) {"
  "  assert.ok(et.length >= 2, `ETag ${et} is well-formed`);"
  "}"
  "// weak prefix"
  "assert.ok(etags[1].startsWith('W/'), ""W/ marks weak ETag"");"
  "assert.ok(!etags[0].startsWith('W/'), ""strong ETag has no prefix"");"
  .

CONDITIONALHEADERSASGUARDS =
  "// ── 3. Conditional headers as guards ─────────────────────────────"
  "const conditionals = ["
  "  ""If-Match"",           // identity guard"
  "  ""If-None-Match"",      // absence guard"
  "  ""If-Modified-Since"",  // time guard"
  "  ""If-Unmodified-Since"",// time guard (inverse)"
  "  ""If-Range"",           // partial guard"
  "];"
  "assert.strictEqual(conditionals.length, 5, ""5 conditionals"");"
  "// the * wildcard"
  "const ifMatchStar = ""If-Match: *"";"
  "const ifNoneMatchStar = ""If-None-Match: *"";"
  "assert.ok(ifMatchStar.includes(""*""),       ""If-Match: * exists"");"
  "assert.ok(ifNoneMatchStar.includes(""*""),   ""If-None-Match: * exists"");"
  "// wildcard semantics"
  "function ifMatchSemantics(value: string, exists: boolean): boolean {"
  "  if (value === ""*"") return exists;"
  "  return false;  // simplified: specific ETag requires match"
  "}"
  "function ifNoneMatchSemantics(value: string, exists: boolean): boolean {"
  "  if (value === ""*"") return !exists;"
  "  return true;"
  "}"
  "assert.strictEqual(ifMatchSemantics(""*"", true),  true,  ""If-Match:* and exists"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(ifMatchSemantics(""*"", false), false, ""If-Match:* and no entity"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(ifNoneMatchSemantics(""*"", true),  false, ""If-None-Match:* and exists"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(ifNoneMatchSemantics(""*"", false), true,  ""If-None-Match:* and no entity"");"
  .

CONTENTRANGEASMODREDUCTION =
  "// ── 4. Content-Range as mod reduction ───────────────────────────"
  "// ""bytes 500-999/1234"" = the range [500, 999] within length 1234"
  "const m = /^bytes (\d+)-(\d+)\/(\d+|\*)$/.exec(""bytes 500-999/1234"");"
  "assert.ok(m !== null, ""Content-Range parses"");"
  "const [, first, last, length] = m!;"
  "assert.strictEqual(Number(first), 500, ""first-byte-pos"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(Number(last),  999, ""last-byte-pos"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(Number(length), 1234, ""instance-length"");"
  "// range is inclusive and ordered"
  "assert.ok(Number(last) >= Number(first), ""last >= first (valid range)"");"
  "// the length is the modulus"
  "assert.ok(Number(first) >= 0 && Number(last) < Number(length), ""range within length"");"
  "// the RFC's examples"
  "const examples = ["
  "  { range: ""bytes 0-499/1234"",   first: 0,    last: 499,  len: 1234 },"
  "  { range: ""bytes 500-999/1234"", first: 500,  last: 999,  len: 1234 },"
  "  { range: ""bytes 500-1233/1234"",first: 500,  last: 1233, len: 1234 },"
  "  { range: ""bytes 734-1233/1234"",first: 734,  last: 1233, len: 1234 },"
  "];"
  "for (const ex of examples) {"
  "  const mm = /^bytes (\d+)-(\d+)\/(\d+)$/.exec(ex.range)!;"
  "  assert.strictEqual(Number(mm[1]), ex.first, `${ex.range} first`);"
  "  assert.strictEqual(Number(mm[2]), ex.last,  `${ex.range} last`);"
  "  assert.strictEqual(Number(mm[3]), ex.len,   `${ex.range} len`);"
  "}"
  .

THETHREELEVELERRORTAXONOMY =
  "// ── 5. The three-level error taxonomy ───────────────────────────"
  "const errors: Record<number, string> = {"
  "  400: ""space"",   // Bad Request"
  "  404: ""frame"",   // Not Found (no matching frame)"
  "  415: ""space"",   // Unsupported Media Type"
  "  416: ""range"",   // Requested Range Not Satisfiable"
  "  417: ""space"",   // Expectation Failed"
  "  500: ""code"",    // Internal Server Error"
  "};"
  "assert.strictEqual(errors[400], ""space"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(errors[404], ""frame"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(errors[416], ""range"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(errors[500], ""code"");"
  .

DATELASTMODIFIEDEXPIRESASTEMPORALFRAMES =
  "// ── 6. Date / Last-Modified / Expires as temporal frames ────────"
  "const temporal = {"
  "  Date:            ""message origination"","
  "  ""Last-Modified"": ""entity last change"","
  "  Expires:         ""cache staleness"","
  "};"
  "assert.deepStrictEqual(Object.keys(temporal).sort(), [""Date"",""Expires"",""Last-Modified""],"
  "  ""three temporal frames"");"
  "// the conditional comparison: Last-Modified vs If-Modified-Since"
  "function isModified(cached: number, current: number): boolean {"
  "  return current > cached;"
  "}"
  "const t0 = Date.parse(""Sat, 29 Oct 1994 19:43:31 GMT"");"
  "const t1 = Date.parse(""Sat, 29 Oct 1994 20:00:00 GMT"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(isModified(t0, t1), true,  ""modified after cache"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(isModified(t1, t0), false, ""not modified before cache"");"
  .

THETHREEREFERENCESMAPTOTHEVAULTSHEADTAILVALUE =
  "// ── 7. The three references map to the vault's (head, tail, value) ─"
  "const mapping = {"
  "  Location:          ""forward ref (head, modulus)"","
  "  ETag:              ""content address (value, invariant under swap)"","
  "  ""Content-Location"":""back ref (tail, prime)"","
  "};"
  "assert.strictEqual(Object.keys(mapping).length, 3, ""3 mappings"");"
  .

THEWILDCARDCONDITION =
  "// ── 8. The wildcard condition ───────────────────────────────────"
  "// ""If-None-Match: *"" is the catch-at-0 condition (I-137):"
  "// perform iff NO entity exists."
  "// ""If-Match: *"" is the dual: perform iff ANY entity exists."
  "function catchAtZero(exists: boolean): boolean { return !exists; }"
  "assert.strictEqual(catchAtZero(false), true,  ""no entity -> perform"");"
  "assert.strictEqual(catchAtZero(true),  false, ""entity exists -> skip"");"
  "console.log(""I-138: HTTP/1.1 three-reference index — passed"");"
  .
